WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.040
For a given task it is often unclear which
attention will do best,

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:05.912
and DARTFormer offers a cheap,

00:00:05.992 --> 00:00:11.592
reliable recipe: train a single-layer
mixed-attention Transformer and use masked validation

00:00:11.672 --> 00:00:13.652
accuracy drop to pick the winner,

00:00:13.732 --> 00:00:19.270
keeping in mind that very low drop scores are a
warning that the choice may be unreliable.

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:22.516
The deeper lesson is a cautionary one for the field.

00:00:22.596 --> 00:00:27.197
Combining diverse attention mechanisms does beat
the average single choice,

00:00:27.277 --> 00:00:29.819
but it never beats the best single choice,

00:00:29.899 --> 00:00:36.810
which suggests the different attentions do not
simply add complementary biases the way common intuition assumes.
